---
// The gallery's "smart layout": cards declare how much room their demo needs
// (ComponentCard's cols/rows) and the grid packs them so the leftovers fill in
// around the big ones - big rocks in the jar first, small rocks into the gaps.
//
// That packing is `grid-auto-flow: row dense` doing the work, not a JS layout
// pass. Dense is exactly the "fill earlier holes with later items that fit"
// algorithm this needs, and getting it from the browser means it re-packs on
// every resize for free, with no measuring, no layout shift, and nothing to
// hydrate. A hand-rolled packer would have to redo all of that worse.
//
// Every row is a fixed 11rem so a span means the same thing on every page. That
// number is set by the demos, not picked for looks: after the card's footer and
// padding, one row leaves 89px of content (the tallest short demo, Number
// Input, needs 74px) and two rows leave 289px (Table needs 281px, Calendar
// 272px, Chart and Tabs 256px). Shrinking it re-introduces scrollbars inside
// the tighter cards.
//
// Note dense packing can move a card ahead of one that precedes it in the DOM,
// so visual order and tab order can disagree. Fine here - each card is a
// self-contained link plus copy button, and nothing about reading one depends
// on the card before it.
---

<div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 auto-rows-[11rem] grid-flow-row-dense">
  <slot />
</div>
